# Cloudflare Pages routing.
#
# The last line is the SPA fallback: a deep link like /remote is not a file, so
# it has to be served index.html and let the router take it from there.
#
# The first line is what stops that fallback answering for the backend. Without
# it, /api/ping returns index.html with a 200 -- and the interface's own
# reachability check read that as "the API is up", rendered the whole workbench,
# and then got this page back from every call it made. A 404 here is the truth:
# there is no API on a static host, and the interface is built to handle being
# told so.
/api/*  /404.html  404
/*      /index.html  200
